# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this repository publishes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intentionally tracked: README.md, TEST_STRATEGY.md, AI_USAGE.md, tests/,
# tools/, notes/, .github/workflows/, Makefile, pyproject.toml,
# requirements-*.txt, service/.
#
# Everything below is either private working material, generated output, or
# machine-local. Nothing here should reach a public repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private working documents — must never be published
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The assignment brief names the hiring company, and the submission checklist
# forbids that name appearing anywhere in the repo.
Staff QA Engineer - Interview Assignment.md
*Interview Assignment*.md

# My own prompt playbook. Working material, not a deliverable.
task.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every knob in this suite is env-driven (see tests/helpers/config.py), so a
# local .env is a realistic thing to create — and exactly the thing not to push.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
credentials.*

